      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, ensure the phone is turned off and unplugged from any power source. Wear rubber gloves and use tools wrapped in a cloth to handle the phone carefully, avoiding direct contact with your hands. Place the phone in a non-conductive container, like a box of styrofoam, and keep it away from flammable materials. Contact your local e-waste recycling center for safe disposal; they have the proper equipment for handling batteries and electronics. Do not reuse the phone or expose it to heat sources. If you notice any signs of overheating, immediately turn off any power sources and contact emergency services.",
